# Network rules management strategy:
# There are two strategies: "allow" and "deny".
# The first network rule indicates the default behavior.
#
# It is recommended to operate in a whitelist mode, allowing specific connections
# and denying all others. This approach enhances security by explicitly specifying
# permitted connections.
#
# However, it is also possible to operate in a blacklist mode, denying specific connections
# and allowing all others. This approach can be useful in scenarios where most connections
# are trusted, and only a few need to be blocked.
#
# Example:
# - In whitelist mode (allow), the first rule might be "deny".
# - In blacklist mode (deny), the first rule might be "allow".

################## Whitelist strategy ##################
# Allow web access
--net=ALLOW|any|0.0.0.0/0|80,443|OUT
--net=ALLOW|any|::/0|80,443|OUT
# TODO Allows HTTP/HTTPS to any IPv6 (Corrected from ::0)


